**Finding: Compliant — no redline needed.**

The agreement contains no non-solicitation, no-hire, or anti-poaching covenant of any kind. Targeted searches for "solicit", "employ", "hire", "induce", "recruit", "personnel", and non-compete language surfaced only:

- **p0051 / p0052** — mutual indemnities referencing third parties "hired by, employed, retained or under" a party's control (allocation of liability, not a hiring restriction);
- **p0061** — confidentiality clause permitting disclosure to employees and directors on a need-to-know basis;
- **p0066** — independent-contractor / no-employment-relationship clause.

None of these restrict The Associated Press from soliciting or hiring Kubient employees. This satisfies our **preferred** position (no non-solicit on Customer), so the fallback (mutual, narrowed, 12-month, general-advertising carve-out) is unnecessary. Worth flagging only defensively: if Kubient later proposes a non-solicit, we should hold to the fallback parameters and reject any no-hire language.
